  "comment": "Regulatory-intelligence objective/mandate layer — FIC. Mirrors the FSCA objective artefact (Regulations/ZA/FSCA/fsca-objective-graph.json). The objective nodes (the 'why' an AML/CFT/CPF requirement exists) are Plane-A reference data, re-derivable from the regulator's own statement of objectives (FIC Act 38/2001 s.3), NOT events (D-REGULATORY-ARCHITECTURE-TWO-PLANE). PURSUES/REFINES/SERVES/ALIGNS_TO edges target EXISTING graph nodes: Regulator REG-FIC (seed-projection.ts Step 1); the FIC Act Document node urn:reg:za:fic-act-38-2001 (seeded by fic-instruments-graph.json — importInstrumentArtefacts runs before importObjectiveArtefacts; ISSUED_BY re-declared here is idempotent); Obligation nodes OBL-ORG-FC-* (Step 6, keyed OBL-<ORG-id>, from Regulations/_obligations.seed.json); Policy nodes POL-<policy-id> (Step 9, from Policies/*.md frontmatter policy-id). SERVES wiring rationale: FIC Act s.3 sets the mandate to combat ML/TF/PF. Four sub-objectives refine it: (1) financial-intelligence is served by the reporting obligations that feed the Centre — CTR/TPR/STR (FC-07/08/09); (2) cdd-integrity is served by the customer-due-diligence, beneficial-ownership, record-keeping and risk-based-approach obligations (FC-02/03/04/05/06/18/19); (3) targeted-sanctions is served by the sanctions / targeted-financial-sanctions screening and freezing obligations (FC-13/14/23/SANCTIONS-SCREENING); (4) aml-supervision is served by the RMCP, MLRO-governance and training obligations (FC-01/11/11-GLOSS-CEO-MLRO-BAR/12/MLRO-ALTERNATE). ALIGNS_TO wiring: the AML/CFT-bundle policies (aml-cft-policy, RMCP-V1, COUNTERPARTY-ONBOARDING-V1, fit-and-proper-policy, ABC-WB-01) align to the cdd-integrity/aml-supervision objectives; the sanctions policy aligns to targeted-sanctions. Every SERVES/ALIGNS_TO target id was confirmed present in the seeded graph (OBL-ORG-FC-* from the seed; POL-* from Policies/*.md frontmatter).",
